# THIS FILE MUST STAND ALONE.
#
# Until 2026-09-09 every rule that actually protected this tree lived in the
# MONOREPO ROOT .gitignore -- `agentic-platform/data/`, `.venv`, `__pycache__/`
# and the rest. That is invisible while you work here, because the root file is
# in effect. It stops being in effect at exactly the wrong moment: the public
# snapshot is a fresh `git init` over a `git archive` of THIS directory, the
# root file does not travel with it, and the first `git add .` would then stage
# a 211 MB `data/` tree containing real tool credentials (data/secrets/*.env),
# the run-token secret and IdP passwords (data/docker.env), SPIRE signing keys
# (data/spire/*/keys.json) and TLS private keys (data/tls/*/key.pem).
#
# So the rules below are deliberately duplicated from the root rather than
# inherited. Do not delete one because "the root already has it": the root is
# the copy that disappears. Anything added here must also hold for a tree with
# no parent directory.

# --- runtime state and secrets -------------------------------------------
# Agent workspaces, minds, local dbs, logs, SPIRE/TLS material, and every
# secret the demos and the IdP need. NOTHING under data/ is ever committed.
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, and it matters: a bare `data/` also matches
# infra/reference-as/data/, whose ceilings.json and users.json are tracked
# fixtures the reference AS needs. An unanchored rule silently dropped them
# from a snapshot simulation.
/data/
.env
# NO blanket `*.env`. It is redundant -- every real secret file lives under
# data/, already excluded above -- and it is harmful: it silently dropped the
# TRACKED demos/enterprise/federated.env, which is platform configuration with
# no secret in it (it references data/secrets/exchange-key.pem by path, and
# that path is excluded). publish/snapshot-gate.py screens env files by name
# and content; this file should not exclude tracked configuration.

# --- locally built binaries ----------------------------------------------
# SPIRE binaries and the per-role executables, built by run.sh rather than
# shipped; see infra/spire/setup-roles.sh.
infra/spire/bin/
infra/roles/

# --- Python build and cache artifacts ------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv
.venv-*/
/build/
/dist/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# --- OS noise ------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store

# --- per-run files the demos generate ------------------------------------
demos/tool-agent/mcp.json
demos/select-tools/mcp.json
demos/tool-agent-http/tool_server.pid
demos/tool-agent-http/tool_server.log

# Generated by ./run.sh sre-demo when it stands its incident up. The MCP config
# is written from the ports the demo actually bound, and the logs are the tool
# servers' own output -- both belong to a run, not to the repo.
demos/sre-triage/mcp.json
demos/sre-triage/logs/
